        "biography": "",
        "appearance": "",
        "notes": "<h5>Tactics</h5><p><strong>Outlaws</strong> rarely fight fair, preferring to ambush and outnumber their targets. Their Ambusher feature gives them an immediate upper hand, allowing them to take shots before their enemies can react. If a fight closes to melee, outlaws use their Roughhousing action to disorient their targets. An outlaw who begins a combat often fights to the death, but if they were caught unawares, they may try to escape—so they can strike again when the advantage is theirs.</p>",
        "role": "minion"
    },
